  "details": "PLEASE VIEW THE FULL DOCUMENT HERE: https://goo.gl/aTcKbb\nThis proposal is in regards to a proposal suggesting the formation of a player-populated “Community Council” for VRChat. This council will serve a very similar purpose to the EVE Online Council of Stellar Management (CSM) system: https://community.eveonline.com/community/csm/. The intent of this Community Council is to advise and assist VRChat developers in the ongoing development of the VRChat platform by providing a more agile and responsive lifeline to the wishes, needs, and goings-on of the VRChat community as a whole.\n\nIn the current state of VRChat, there is relatively limited communication between VRChat decision-makers and the community. Although the Canny provides a message-board style communication format, it is often not reflective of the current state of the community. Additionally, the communication is often (but not always) uni-directional. For example, if the community requests a change, it can be addressed within the Canny. However, changes implemented by the developers ad-hoc during the beta process may be done without consulting with the community at all, potentially causing unintended impacts that the VRChat developers may not be aware of.\n\nThe Community Council serves to solve that problem by providing a processing and content filter for the developers. Because these council members would be members of the community themselves, they would be immersed in the general attitude and feel of the community as a whole. This would allow easy “translation” of the current community goings-on, the strongest wants and needs, the greatest praises, and the loudest complaints into an easy-to-digest format for the development team. \n\nAs it stands, we believe that five members would suffice to fill the Community Council management team. The community would vote on these members in a standard election process, solidified with approval from the VRChat team. These members would serve a time-based term (say, 6 months or a year) and then their slot would open for re-election.\n\nThe goal of the VRChat Community Council is to facilitate and foster productive discussion and feedback between the VRChat community-at-large and the VRChat development team-- in particular, the team members who have the responsibility to make decisions on the future of VRChat. If VRChat is going to become what it aspires to be-- a VR metaverse akin to Ready Player One’s Oasis, then community feedback is vital. Without knowledge of the current happenings and trends of the creator community, it can be very difficult to make effective and meaningful decisions that benefit everyone involved.\n\nConsidering that VRChat is extremely heavily reliant on the creative community and their ability to exercise their considerable skills (to the benefit of VRChat’s content), this cycle of discussion, feedback, and action should prove wildly useful to the development of VRChat. It is the hope of the authors of this document that the proposal will be taken into serious consideration, and VRChat will work with the authors to help smooth this system into something that can work for all of us.",
